        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 9 at 2:58PM PST until November 10 at 12:00PM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Minor to locally moderate coastal flooding expected.\nAdditionally, dangerous rip currents and surf of 3 to 6 feet\nexpected along west-facing beaches.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...For the Coastal Flood Advisory, until noon PST Tuesday.\nFor the Beach Hazards Statement, through Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of parking lots and roads with only\nisolated road closures expected. Dangerous swimming conditions\ndue to elevated surf and strong rip currents.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...High tide Tuesday morning is expected to\npeak over 7 feet MLLW, which is 1.2 to 1.4 feet above\nastronomical tide predictions. Higher surf today could prolong\ncoastal impacts.",
        "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.\n\nRemain out of the water to avoid hazardous swimming conditions.",
